  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant modality (0.48-0.52 vs 0.21 for image-only), and scvi_n200 (0.5203) outperforms pca_n2000 (0.4849) by ~3.5%, showing that learned RNA representations matter. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested scgpt, the third available RNA encoder, and it may provide a substantially better or comparable representation. Question: config_007 (scgpt, singleprofile, rna_only) isolates the effect of the RNA encoder while holding profile setting and model setting constant, giving a clean three-way comparison (pca vs scvi vs scgpt). Why this is the best next experiment: Resolving which RNA encoder is strongest is the most fundamental design choice before investing the remaining 6 experiments in multiprofile or multimodal configurations. If scgpt is significantly better, all subsequent experiments should build on it; if it is comparable to or worse than scvi_n200, we confirm scvi as the backbone and can pivot to testing multiprofile or multimodal fusion in the next round. This single experiment reduces the most critical uncertainty at minimal cost."
}

